From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Writer inserts a filled table, the cursor kept

- .uno:ElyInsertTable (Cells, After, Header) inserts a table after the
  body's last block, or after the block holding After's first body match,
  in one undo step, without moving any view's cursor or selection.
- Cells holds rows split by U+001E and cells split by U+001F; every row
  needs the same number of cells. Header "true" makes the first row a
  heading row repeated on each page.
- At the body's end a plain paragraph follows the table, as Writer keeps.
- Uneven rows or no match leave the document as it was.

